  0 ...
  The ADL monitors 10,000 spaces a day
  and feeds all that data into the OHI V3
  that analyzes it in real time to identify
  you by your voice.
  For private subscription spaces, they
  use their backdoor through CHEQ.
  2:55 PM • Nov 3, 2025 • 217 Views
  1
  176
  19
  4
  Post your reply
  Reply
  1984 @TheOfficial1984 • 4h
  They also tie your voice to a
  geolocation.
  2. Audio Transcription:
  • Raw audio from Spaces is transcribed using
  speech-to-text models, often leveraging third-
  party services like Google's Speech-to-Text or
  open-source alternatives (e.g., Whisper from
  OpenAl). This step converts spoken words into
  timestamped text transcripts, preserving context
  like speaker turns and pauses. Accuracy is around
  85-95% for English, lower for accents or noisy
  environments, leading to potential false positives.
  • Metadata such as speaker identification (via voice
  biometrics in advanced setups) and geolocation
  (if enabled) is captured to contextualize the
  content.
  © 15 ill 193 1
  1984 @TheOfficial1984 • 4h
  This is how your score is calculated.
  •..
  • The transcribed text is fed into OHI V3's core
  model, a fine-tuned transformer-based neural
  network (built on architectures like BERT or
  RoBERTa). The model evaluates:
  • Semantic Analysis: Detects implicit bias,
  dog-whistles (e.g., coded references to
  conspiracy theories), and intersectional hate
  (e.g., antisemitism combined with racism).
  • Contextual Scoring: Considers surrounding
  dialogue; isolated phrases are cross-
  reterenced with the tull transcriot to avoid
  misclassitication.A
  • Thresholding: Content scoring above 0.9
  (high confidence) triggers alerts. V3
  improves on prior versions by incorporating
  multilingual support (e.g., Arabic, Spanish)
  and reducing bias against non-English
